% An alternative of a type definition may be a TYPE NAME, giving the union of
% types with disjoint top-level functors (TGLP typed-glp.tex).  The automaton
% inherits the named type's transitions (appendix sec:type-automaton, "Type
% definition transitions"); it used to build none at all for such an
% alternative, so a(N, _) had no transition from state T? and this file did not
% load.  Reported by Currencies Code, 2026-09-03.
T ::= A ; b.
A ::= a(Integer, Constant).
exported procedure take(T?, Integer).
take(a(N, _), N?).
take(b, 0).
